  "instructions": {
    "text_instructions": [
      {
        "id": "01f1cade55191748a28e058c00230c99",
        "content": [
          "This Space answers questions about FEMA Public Assistance (PA) grant projects that have been financially obligated to recipients. Each row is one funded project worksheet for one applicant under one disaster declaration.\n",
          "\n",
          "Key definitions, use these when interpreting questions:\n",
          "\n",
          "- \"Obligated\" means FEMA has committed the funding to the grantee (the state). Projects still in pre-obligation processing are not in this data.\n",
          "- `federalShareObligated` is the federal money made available to the grantee. This is usually what people mean by \"how much FEMA funded.\"\n",
          "- `totalObligated` is the federal share plus state and applicant administrative costs. The federal share is typically 75% of total project cost.\n",
          "- `projectAmount` is the estimated total project cost from the damage survey, before admin costs. It is an estimate, not the obligated figure.\n",
          "- `mitigationAmount` is the portion applied to 406 hazard mitigation. It can be negative due to adjustments; do not treat negatives as errors.\n",
          "- When a user asks \"how much was awarded / funded / obligated,\" default to summing `federalShareObligated` unless they say otherwise.\n",
          "- `damageCategoryCode` is a single letter. Categories A-B are emergency work (debris, protective measures); C-G are permanent work (roads, water control, buildings, utilities, parks). Use `damageCategoryDescrip` for the human-readable label.\n",
          "- `projectSize` is either Large or Small, set by the eligible dollar amount in the damage survey.\n",
          "- `stateAbbreviation` is the two-letter state/territory code. `county` is the applicant location; it may be blank for tribal or territorial applicants.\n",
          "\n",
          "Financial caveat to surface when relevant: this data comes from FEMA's Grants Manager (FAC-Trax), not FEMA's official financial system, so totals may differ slightly from USAspending.gov. It is not for official federal reporting.\n",
          "\n",
          "Always report dollar figures rounded to whole dollars with a thousands separator. When grouping by state or county, order results by the summed federal share descending unless asked otherwise."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "example_question_sqls": [
      {
        "id": "01f1cb27609011a0a077d2ee1859a2c4",
        "question": [
          "Top 5 counties by federal share for a given state with emergency vs permanent work split"
        ],
        "sql": [
          "SELECT county, COUNT(*) AS projects, SUM(CASE WHEN damageCategoryCode IN ('A','B') THEN federalShareObligated ELSE 0 END) AS emergency_work_funding, SUM(CASE WHEN damageCategoryCode IN ('C','D','E','F','G') THEN federalShareObligated ELSE 0 END) AS permanent_work_funding, SUM(federalShareObligated) AS total_federal_share FROM workspace.default.funded_projects_details WHERE stateAbbreviation = 'FL' AND county IS NOT NULL AND county != '' GROUP BY county ORDER BY total_federal_share DESC LIMIT 5"
        ]
      }
    ],
